  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Complete robust multituberculate with broad rodent-like head, enlarged incisors and heavy grinding jaws. Not a rodent/beaver or isolated skull. [\"2025 original postcranial study assigns robust ulna/radius/femur/calcaneus but acknowledges incomplete skeleton; ground-dwelling inferred, digging only possible not established.\", \"Exact torso, tail, digits and soft tissue proportions not fossil-established; conservative reconstruction only.\", \"Fur color and ears speculative. Do not conflate multituberculate with modern Rodentia.\", \"2021 composite skull drawing combines several fossils; not one complete exact specimen scan.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"skull_condylobasal_length_m\": 0.161, \"skull_bizygomatic_width_m\": 0.146, \"basis\": \"2021 Table5 DMNH EPV.95284; authors caution measurements >50mm are rounded estimates because of deformation/breakage. 153.3mm cranial size is geometric mean, NOT skull length. AMNH16321 length159mm,width155mm,cranialsize157mm.\", \"head_body_length_m\": 0.65, \"tail_length_m\": 0.2, \"shoulder_height_m\": 0.28, \"whole_body_status\": \"Conservative artistic reconstruction dimensions; no complete articulated skeleton supports exact whole length.\", \"soft_tissue_note\": \"Reference dimensions constrain broad cranial proportions, not an exact fossil surface fit. External soft-tissue head is larger than the bony skull. Head/body/shoulder values are design estimates; exact exported bounds are recorded in technical evidence.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：Complete robust multituberculate with broad rodent-like head, enlarged incisors and heavy grinding jaws. Not a rodent/beaver or isolated skull. [\"2025 original postcranial study assigns robust ulna/radius/femur/calcaneus but acknowledges incomplete skeleton; ground-dwelling inferred, digging only possible not established.\", \"Exact torso, tail, digits and soft tissue proportions not fossil-established; conservative reconstruction only.\", \"Fur color and ears speculative. Do not conflate multituberculate with modern Rodentia.\", \"2021 composite skull drawing combines several fossils; not one complete exact specimen scan.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"skull_condylobasal_length_m\": 0.161, \"skull_bizygomatic_width_m\": 0.146, \"basis\": \"2021 Table5 DMNH EPV.95284; authors caution measurements >50mm are rounded estimates because of deformation/breakage. 153.3mm cranial size is geometric mean, NOT skull length. AMNH16321 length159mm,width155mm,cranialsize157mm.\", \"head_body_length_m\": 0.65, \"tail_length_m\": 0.2, \"shoulder_height_m\": 0.28, \"whole_body_status\": \"Conservative artistic reconstruction dimensions; no complete articulated skeleton supports exact whole length.\", \"soft_tissue_note\": \"Reference dimensions constrain broad cranial proportions, not an exact fossil surface fit. External soft-tissue head is larger than the bony skull. Head/body/shoulder values are design estimates; exact exported bounds are recorded in technical evidence.\"}"
  },
